.TH SDL_enabled_assert 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_enabled_assert \- The macro used when an assertion is enabled.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_assert.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_enabled_assert(condition) \(rs
.BI "    do { \(rs
.BI "        while ( !(condition) ) { \(rs
.BI "            static struct SDL_AssertData sdl_assert_data = { false, 0, #condition, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL }; \(rs
.BI "            const SDL_AssertState sdl_assert_state = SDL_ReportAssertion(&sdl_assert_data, SDL_FUNCTION, SDL_ASSERT_FILE, SDL_LINE); \(rs
.BI "            if (sdl_assert_state == SDL_ASSERTION_RETRY) { \(rs
.BI "                continue; /* go again. */ \(rs
.BI "            } else if (sdl_assert_state == SDL_ASSERTION_BREAK) { \(rs
.BI "                SDL_AssertBreakpoint(); \(rs
.BI "            } \(rs
.BI "            break; /* not retrying. */ \(rs
.BI "        } \(rs
.BI "    } while (SDL_NULL_WHILE_LOOP_CONDITION)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This isn\(aqt for direct use by apps, but this is the code that is inserted when an
.BR SDL_assert
is enabled\[char46]
.PP
The
.BR "do {} while(0)"
avoids dangling else problems:

.IP
.EX
if (x) SDL_assert(y); else blah();
.EE
.PP

\[char46]\[char46]\[char46] without the do/while, the \(dqelse\(dq could attach to this macro\(aqs \(dqif\(dq\[char46] We try to handle just the minimum we need here in a macro\[char46]\[char46]\[char46]the loop, the static vars, and break points\[char46] The heavy lifting is handled in
.BR SDL_ReportAssertion ()\[char46]

.SH MACRO PARAMETERS
.TP
.I condition
the condition to assert\[char46]
.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

